Subject: [PATCH 2/3] db-check: the review's two gaps and two nits
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An independent review of the previous commit found no blocking defect. It
confirmed:
- nothing in the repository inserts into the capability log as erp_app or
  erp_edge, and a direct insert as erp_edge is now refused;
- the wrapper is safe for all 56 assertion runs;
- the image the CLI pins keeps no routine, type or sequence in public;
- the migration header's claims hold;
- its regex agrees with a fuller tokenizer on all 78 definer routes the
  runtime may call, and on 4,000 random bodies.

It found two low gaps, both fixed here.

L2. The runner's wrapper trimmed only spaces in SQL while the reader
trimmed all whitespace, so a violation of nothing but a tab or a no-break
space still read as none. Each row is now read after a record separator,
chr(30), and split on it, so a row counts whatever its text, and a
violation over two lines is one row, not two.

L1. The gate check's description claimed it read comments and strings as
the parser does. It now strips quoted identifiers too, so an apostrophe or
"--" inside one no longer hides a call and a mention inside one is not a
call. A line comment now ends at a carriage return as well as a newline, as
PostgreSQL's scanner reads it. Every branch starts with a different
character, so leftmost-longest matching cannot pick a wrong one. What a
regular expression cannot read is now said, in the check's description and
in CLAUDE.md: a nested comment, a backslash-escaped quote in an E'' string,
and a dollar-quoted string. No route has one.

The nits:
- 0025 says the owner bypasses row security, which is why it never needed
  the dropped policy, not that the policy named another role;
- ADR-0022's addendum quotes 0011's note on its privileges, not its header.

The controls grow to match:
- six blank, whitespace-only and two-line violations read as six;
- the mention-only route also hides the gate in a quoted identifier;
- the gated route calls it after an identifier with an apostrophe and a
  comment ended by a bare carriage return.

Eight copies of the tree each reverted one piece, and db:check failed with
exactly the matching check:
- 0025 removed;
- the old public query;
- the old strpos;
- the old line-based runner;
- comments stripped before strings;
- no identifier branch;
- a line comment ending only at a newline;
- the first btrim wrapper.

These pass:
- npm run db:check (133);
- db:fixtures;
- every pgTAP suite but 040 (010 19/19, 060 21/21);
- verify (695 tests);
- secret:scan;
- dep:policy.

Requirements: CAP-P03 · CAP-P04 · SEC-006

